    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">Part 2</div>
      <h2>The Email Assistant Prompt</h2>
      <p>One structured prompt, built on the CTSTF framework, for consistent daily email triage.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="price-card" style="max-width:100%;">
      <p style="color:#DCE3EC; font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.85; font-family:var(--sans);">
        <strong style="color:var(--gold-soft);">CONTEXT:</strong> You are helping me triage my inbox. I receive a mix of client requests, internal admin, and low-priority updates.<br><br>
        <strong style="color:var(--gold-soft);">TASK:</strong> For each email I paste, tell me: (1) urgency — high/medium/low, (2) what action it needs, if any, (3) a one-line draft reply if it's routine enough to answer immediately.<br><br>
        <strong style="color:var(--gold-soft);">STANDARDS:</strong> Don't invent context I haven't given you. If you're unsure of urgency, say so and ask rather than guessing.<br><br>
        <strong style="color:var(--gold-soft);">TONE:</strong> Match my reply draft to the sender's own tone — formal in, formal out.<br><br>
        <strong style="color:var(--gold-soft);">FORMAT:</strong> Urgency / Action Needed / Draft Reply (if applicable) — three short lines, nothing else.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">Part 3</div>
      <h2>The 5-Minute Client Intake Workflow</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Step 1 — Capture the raw notes</h4>
        <p>During or right after a client call, jot down rough, unstructured notes — don't worry about format at all.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Step 2 — Structure it in one prompt</h4>
        <p>"Turn these rough intake notes into a structured case summary with: client goals, key facts, open questions, and next steps." Paste your notes after it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Step 3 — Generate the follow-up</h4>
        <p>"Based on this structured summary, draft a short follow-up email confirming what we discussed and next steps." This becomes your client-facing confirmation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Step 4 — File it</h4>
        <p>Save the structured summary (not the raw notes) into your case file — consistent formatting means anyone on your team can pick up the file and understand it immediately.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

